{
  "source": "Independent analytic construction, not RotationModel/CPU/GPU output",
  "radiusMeters": 6371000,
  "coordinateConvention": "longitude/latitude in degrees; right-handed positive rotation about geographic north; longitude normalized to [-180,180)",
  "derivation": [
    "North pole is the +z axis. A positive angle theta rotates the equatorial x/y vector; longitude increases by theta and latitude is unchanged.",
    "Model A: theta101(t)=theta102(t)=0. Model B for 0<=t<=100: theta101(t)=0.9*t degrees; theta102(t)=0.3*t degrees.",
    "Relative to anchor a, subtract theta_a: theta_relative=theta_moving-theta_anchor, theta0=0. At t=50, moving101/anchor102 is 45-15=30 degrees.",
    "At t=100, moving101/anchor102 is 90-30=60 degrees. Starting (20,30) gives (80,30). Starting (170,-20) anchored0 gives wrap(260)=-100 degrees longitude."
  ],
  "toleranceDegrees": 1e-08,
